# MoveCartesianPoseSequence Service Definition
#
# Executes an arbitrary sequence of Cartesian poses via MoveIt's Cartesian path planner.
# Unlike /move_cartesian_sequence which requires named waypoints from YAML,
# this service accepts geometry_msgs/PoseStamped[] directly.
#
# Request:
#   - poses: List of Cartesian waypoints to visit in sequence (PoseStamped[]).
#             Poses should normally be in base_link frame.
#             If frame_id is empty, defaults to "base_link".
#             If orientation is all zeros, replaced with the calibrated default orientation.
#   - execute: If true, plan and execute the Cartesian path.
#              If false, plan only.
#
# Response:
#   - success: True if planning (and execution if requested) succeeded.
#   - message: Human-readable result/diagnostic message.
#   - fraction: MoveIt Cartesian path fraction (0.0 to 1.0).

geometry_msgs/PoseStamped[] poses
bool execute
---
bool success
string message
float64 fraction
